  "prefLabel": "En 1002.50 Spot network",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1002.50 “Spot network” means a section of an electric delivery system that uses 2 or more inter-tied transformers to supply an electrical network circuit. A spot network is generally used to supply power to a single utility customer or to a small group of utility customers and has the same meaning as the term is used in IEEE Std 1547™-2018, “IEEE Standard for Interconnection and Interoperability of Distributed Energy Resources with Associated Electric Power System Interfaces” dated 4/6/2018.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
